    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 49 Willow Park Grove is a substantial four bedroom detached family home. Lovingly maintained by the same family for many years, this impressive home now offers its next owners the superb opportunity to modernise and create a truly outstanding family home tailored to their own tastes and requirements.\n\nThe accommodation comprises of a large welcoming entrance hall with walk in understairs storage. To the right is a spacious reception room that could serve multiple uses, while to the left lies the bright dual aspect open plan living/ dining room which overlooks the beautiful rear garden. The kitchen is filled with natural light and completes the ground floor accommodation. Upstairs, there are four generously proportioned bedrooms arranged around a spacious landing. A shower room and separate WC complete the accommodation. \n\nA standout feature of No. 49 is its exceptional south facing rear garden. Bathed in sunlight throughout the day, this private outdoor space provides the perfect setting for family life, entertaining and relaxation. Laid mainly in lawn and bordered by mature trees, established hedging and colourful planting, it offers a rare sense of privacy and seclusion. \nAdding further practicality, the garden benefits from direct access to the large attached side garage, providing excellent storage, workshop space or potential for conversion (subject to planning).\n \nThe location is excellent being within walking distance of countless amenities and convenient to numerous shops, cafes, bars and restaurants. Dublin City University and Albert College Park are both within short walking distance, with a variety of sports clubs including Na Fianna and a great selection of national and secondary schools locally. The Four Courts, Beaumont Hospital and the Mater Hospital are all within easy reach. Commuting further afield is made very easy with the M50 Motorway, the M1 and Dublin Airport within a few minutes' drive. The area is very well serviced by public transport, through the many bus routes which pass close by.\n\nIf you would like a viewing of this property, please email us at Drumcondra@sherryfitz.ie or call the office directly on 018373737 to arrange an appointment. If you wish to place an offer, please visit www.sherryfitz.ie where you can register to make an offer on this property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4.58m x 2.04m\nLarge welcoming entrance hall with understairs storage space.\n\nLiving/ Dining Room - 7.46m x 3.78m\nSuperb open plan dual aspect room overlooking the rear garden, with solid fuel stove and door to rear garden.\n\nKitchen - 4.88m x 4.70m\nWith wall and floor units, an abundance of countertop space and door to rear garden.\n\nFamily Room - 3.32m x 2.58m\nSpacious room with carpet flooring that could serve multiple uses.\n\nLanding - 5.86m x 1.92m\nWith carpet flooring and attic hatch leading up to a large attic space complete with tongue and groove flooring and window.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.32m x 3.66m\nLarge dual double bedroom with carpet flooring and built in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.92m x 3.04m\nDouble bedroom with carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.02m x 2.58m\nDouble bedroom with carpet flooring and built in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.32m x 2.26m\nSpacious bedroom with carpet flooring and built in wardrobe.\n\nShower Room - 2.42m x 1.58m\nWith tiled walls, wc and shower.\n\nWC - 1.50m x 0.84m\nWith tiled walls and wc.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Substantial detached four bed family home</li><li>Overlooking large green to the front</li><li>Exceptional sunny south facing rear garden</li><li>Extra large floored attic space with window</li><li>Gas fired central heating </li><li>Large attached side garage</li><li>Ample off street parking </li><li>Walking distance of DCU and excellent selection of schools </li><li>Short drive to M1, M50 and Dublin Airport</ul>"
      },
